 "note": "DEVELOPMENT DATA, POST HOC, NO MODEL CALLS. e1v2_abstention_policies.py scores the policies \"hold to a deadline (q)\" and \"recheck, source stale with probability p\" with one seeded draw per case-repeat, so their reported rates are single draws. Both policies are mixtures of deterministic outcomes per case-repeat with no reading:   hold_deadline_q    = q * (recheck with the true source) + (1 - q) * (standing plan)   recheck_stale_p    = (1 - p) * (recheck with the true source) + p * (recheck that returns                        the value in force before the notice) and every case-repeat with a reading is decided as under every other policy. This tool computes the three deterministic outcomes for every case-repeat, with the same functions as e1v2_abstention_policies.py, and reports the exact expected violations per change notice and delivered shares. It also re-derives the seeded draws, as a check that the outcomes match the stored policy results. Raised by the pre-submission review of the AI4Factory paper (manuscripts/aaai-workshop/REVIEW-2026-11-16.md, row 10). ",
